    {
      "id": "smart-government-applications-powered-by-digital-wallets-HCB5DD",
      "sector": "public_sector",
      "title": "Smart Government Applications Powered by Digital Wallets",
      "summary": "Our award‑winning Wallet‑Centric Public‑Service Platform proves that modern G2B service delivery in the Netherlands is achievable today. Built with real governmental issuers and relying parties, it uses a Key Life‑Event architecture and provides validated feasibility, reusable components, and a funded roadmap.\n\nThe platform brings together core public actors and applies digital business and personal wallets with responsible agentic AI. Its modular, wallet‑agnostic design enables scalable innovation.\n\nThe first use case helps entrepreneurs find and apply for subsidies and funding as one recurring life event. Secure wallets and AI guidance reduce complexity, errors, and incomplete submissions.\n\nThe governance model began in a Public‑Private‑Academic hackathon (2025) and now advances through a governmental partnership supported by the Digital Government Innovation Budget grant (2026).\n\nThe solution prevents fragmented information, repeated data entry, and non‑compliant applications. Entrepreneurs gain faster, accurate support and control over verified data; government agencies receive complete, reliable submissions and fewer manual processes. The approach is transferable across domain",
      "organizationName": "Kamer van Koophandel",
      "productionDeployment": "no",
      "status": "published",
